=== A. HEAT CONTENT AND PHONONS (diamond)
  Debye temperature solved from the measured value, not fitted to anything else:
    from Cp(298.16 K) = 6.1149 J/(mol K) [DeSorbo 1953, NIST WebBook], taking Cp = Cv:  Theta_D = 1861.0444 K
    from S(298.15 K) = 2.3782 J/(mol K) [DeSorbo 1953]:                                  Theta_D = 1864.7455 K
    the two differ by 0.1989 % : the Debye model is not exact for diamond (one optical branch at 1332.7 cm^-1); both are model-defined numbers
  [Cp] k Theta_D = 0.1603724 eV; heat content U(298.15)-U(0) per gram = 43.636776 J (per mol 523.64131); fraction of M c^2 = 4.85525e-13; zero-point (9/8) k Theta per atom = 0.18041895 eV, per gram 1450.6485 J
      cycles of one phonon quantum at the lattice constant: a k Theta/(hbar c) = 0.00028988489 ; at the C-C bond: 0.00012552384
  [S] k Theta_D = 0.16069133 eV; heat content U(298.15)-U(0) per gram = 43.422055 J (per mol 521.06466); fraction of M c^2 = 4.83136e-13; zero-point (9/8) k Theta per atom = 0.18077775 eV, per gram 1453.5334 J
      cycles of one phonon quantum at the lattice constant: a k Theta/(hbar c) = 0.00029046138 ; at the C-C bond: 0.00012577347
  Raman zone-centre optical phonon 1332.7 +- 0.2 cm^-1 (0 K) = 0.16523374 eV (secondary source); cycles at the C-C bond: 0.00012932882 ; Raman energy / k Theta_D(Cp): 1.03031 ; Raman energy / kT(298.15 K): 6.43119
  modes in the gram: 3 N = 1.505535191e+23 ; cycles of one Debye quantum at the C-C bond: 0.000125524 ; Debye thermal energy per mode at 298.15 K: 0.00180905 eV
  hbar c / k Theta_D (Cp) wavelength-scale of the cutoff phonon: 1.2304298e-6 m =  26.7625 p12

=== B. GRAPHITE vs DIAMOND (graphite density, in-plane bond and interlayer are search-result quotations; entropies from the saved NIST page)
  diamond: V 2.846603e-7 m^3, R_sph 0.0040808074 m, p12 30.02483 , BC cycles 1.1600872e+37 , bits 1.0515866e+38
  graphite (2.267 g/cm^3): V 4.411116e-7 m^3, R_sph 0.0047222969 m, p12 30.08359 , BC cycles 1.3424491e+37 , bits 1.2168926e+38 ; radius ratio g/d 1.1571967
  graphite-like entropy Takahashi-Westrum 1970 (amorphous label): 5.833 J/(mol K) -> per gram 5.079278e+22 bits ; ratio to diamond 2.4527 ; BC bits / thermodynamic bits 2.3958e+15 (decades 15.3795)
  graphite-like entropy Lutcov et al. 1970: 6.201 J/(mol K) -> per gram 5.3997262e+22 bits ; ratio to diamond 2.60743 ; BC bits / thermodynamic bits 2.25362e+15 (decades 15.3529)
  diamond: thermodynamic bits 2.0708965e+22 ; decades gap 15.7057
  bond cycles: diamond C-C 1.54448e-10 m with E = Ec/2 = 3.68553 eV (2 bonds per atom, 4 neighbours) -> 0.0028846759 ; graphite in-plane C-C 1.42e-10 with E = Ec/1.5 = 4.91405 eV (3 neighbours, 1.5 bonds per atom) -> 0.0035362346
  (Ec is the 0 K atomic enthalpy of formation, one number for both: the difference between graphite and diamond cohesion, ~2 kJ/mol, is below the printed digits and is not applied)
  graphite interlayer 3.35e-10 m -> 23.459 p12; in-plane/interlayer = 0.423881

