=== D. NUCLEAR MATTER RADIUS from the charge radius (arithmetic with PDG 2024 inputs)
  inputs: r_ch(12C) = 2.4702 fm (secondary), r_p = 0.8409 fm (PDG 2024), <r_n^2> = -0.1155(17) fm^2 (PDG 2024), Darwin-Foldy 3/4 (hbar/m_p c)^2 = 0.0331724 fm^2
  point-proton r_pp^2 = r_ch^2 - r_p^2 - (N/Z)<r_n^2> - DF = 5.4771029 fm^2 -> r_pp = 2.3403211 fm
  with N = Z and isospin symmetry (Coulomb and the spin-orbit term for 12C neglected) the point-matter radius equals r_pp:  2.34032 fm  (ratio to r_ch 0.947422 )
  nucleus cycles B r/(hbar c) with r_ch                  : 1.153709026 ; p12 of the radius 18.7033
  nucleus cycles B r/(hbar c) with r_pp (matter, point)  : 1.093048974 ; p12 of the radius 18.6815
  nuclear matter radius shifts the nucleus cycles by -5.258 % (the comparison with the nucleon r_p/lambda_p = 3.9977 and the A^(4/3) growth is unchanged in kind)

